GHC 6.2.2 -- mhs: T(..) does not import an abstract type's field selectors
Several modules export a type abstractly and its field selectors by name
(HscTypes.IfaceDecls, TyCon.TyCon, Var.varType); GHC lets an importer's
`T(..)` pick the selectors up, MicroHs does not, so they are named
explicitly. Conversely where a module needs a type's constructors
(ForeignCall, Type, MonoBinds) the import says `T(..)`. Two comment-only
edits (Unique{-instance NamedThing-} in PprAbsC and RnIfaces) came from
the same substitution and are kept for byte fidelity.

